++//! The established part of a metallib's `SPCI` to `SLST` specialization association.
++//!
++//! An empty-library `SPCI` names a base by the 32-byte `HASH` of a named function, then names a
++//! script group by its offset from the start of the `SLST` section. This reader validates that
++//! complete association without assigning semantics to the script itself. It does not flatten an
++//! alias onto its base: each binding retains the function's own bitcode and verified hash, and
++//! its base named function separately.
++//!
++//! `SLST` groups are consumed from their count word through the section end. A group's `u32` size
++//! counts that size word, and its tag list ends exactly at the group end. `SBUF` is the
++//! uncompressed-script token: its `u32` size covers the payload and its leading zero padding to a
++//! 16-byte boundary from the MTLB start. `SBUZ` and `RBUZ` remain opaque, as do unknown tags.
++
++use std::collections::BTreeMap;
++
++use super::tags::RawTag;
++use super::{container_error, Hash256, Metallib, SpecializationConstants};
++use crate::error::{ContainerError, Error};
